WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.100
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.105 --> 00:01.105
MkvDrama.net

3
00:03.108 --> 00:05.360
[rustling]

4
00:05.444 --> 00:08.196
-[moaning in distance] -Hmm?

5
00:12.534 --> 00:16.747
[Satoshi] Stink bugs, stink bugs! That squishy white offal.

6
00:21.335 --> 00:24.921
Broad beans, broad beans, broad beans, broad beans!

7
00:25.005 --> 00:28.633
-Broad beans. -[both panting, moaning]

8
00:31.803 --> 00:33.305
Who's a broad bean?

9
00:35.057 --> 00:36.725
I read it online.

10
00:37.184 --> 00:41.730
"When you're about to finish, think of things you hate to last longer."

11
00:42.481 --> 00:45.484
-Then you don't have to say it out loud. -[soft chuckle]

12
00:48.236 --> 00:50.906
Chiko, how was today's?

13
00:50.989 --> 00:54.534
I don't know! How many times has this happened today?

14
01:05.837 --> 01:06.880
[exclaims]

15
01:08.173 --> 01:09.925
My shift got canceled today.

16
01:10.759 --> 01:12.803
[Chiko] Without it even raining?

17
01:13.804 --> 01:17.974
Yeah, it's about the construction schedule changing.

18
01:18.058 --> 01:19.142
Mm.

19
01:19.226 --> 01:20.727
[deep inhale]

20
01:20.811 --> 01:24.564
Man, part-time jobs are so unstable.

21
01:25.107 --> 01:27.109
[Chiko] Then won't you come help me out?

22
01:28.151 --> 01:33.990
BIG ZAM'S DAILY LUNCH SPECIAL

23
01:35.867 --> 01:37.828
I kept you waiting.

24
01:41.123 --> 01:44.292
Presenting Mr. Karaage No. 1.

25
01:44.376 --> 01:46.086
The seasoning is a secret.

26
01:46.628 --> 01:49.005
We're in the middle of a massive karaage boom.

27
01:49.089 --> 01:51.842
No, a karaage war!

28
01:52.384 --> 01:57.264
You're gonna rob every last coin from people passing by.

29
01:57.347 --> 01:58.723
Pretty genius, right?

30
01:58.807 --> 02:02.060
A karaage boom? Talk about jumping on the bandwagon late.

31
02:02.144 --> 02:05.021
A businessman never walks away empty-handed,

32
02:05.105 --> 02:08.650
and an Osaka native never lets anyone get something for free.

33
02:09.276 --> 02:13.280
You're gonna pay back the trouble you caused your mom here.

34
02:13.363 --> 02:16.950
Don't slack off, or else.

35
02:18.034 --> 02:19.828
-Got it. -Good!

36
02:22.831 --> 02:26.918
Welcome! Get your karaage here!

37
02:27.002 --> 02:30.505
Ah! "Mr. Karaage"! Branding is important.

38
02:30.589 --> 02:31.631
Got it.

39
02:31.715 --> 02:32.883
[Hironi] Good! I trust you!

40
02:32.966 --> 02:34.885
Right. Welcome!

41
02:34.968 --> 02:37.929
Get your Mr. Karaage here!

42
02:38.013 --> 02:39.514
-Satoshi. -Yes.

43
02:39.598 --> 02:41.933
-I'm sorry. -[chuckles] No, not at all.

44
02:42.017 --> 02:43.226
Actually, I'm happy.

45
02:43.310 --> 02:46.188
It's been a while since we worked together, right?

46
02:46.271 --> 02:47.606
Here, Chiko.

47
02:47.689 --> 02:51.777
Come on, you too! Say "Yes!" Ready?

48
02:52.527 --> 02:55.822
Welcome! Fresh-fried karaage!

49
02:55.906 --> 02:57.199
Add "Mr."

50
02:57.282 --> 03:00.118
[both] Fresh-fried Mr. Karaage!

51
03:01.369 --> 03:02.496
-Kara-- -Interested?

52
03:02.579 --> 03:04.831
[customer] One extra-large. How much?

53
03:04.915 --> 03:08.001
[Satoshi] Thank you! One extra-large. How much?

54
03:08.084 --> 03:09.085
-[Chiko] Not priced. -[Satoshi] Right.

55
03:09.169 --> 03:10.170
RED LIGHT ELEGY

56
03:10.754 --> 03:14.382
1,000 yen, 9,000 yen, full. 4,000 yen.

57
03:14.466 --> 03:15.717
EPISODE 5

58
03:15.801 --> 03:18.261
Make this a weekly thing?

59
03:18.345 --> 03:21.014
Include staff meals.

60
03:21.097 --> 03:23.475
Only 500 yen each.

61
03:23.558 --> 03:25.018
Wait, not on the house?

62
03:25.101 --> 03:27.020
Hironi, it's not cooked.

63
03:27.103 --> 03:28.563
[Hironi] Medium-rare!

64
03:29.397 --> 03:31.233
-Hell no. -[door opens]

65
03:31.316 --> 03:33.276
-[customer] Coming in. -Hi, welcome!

66
03:38.865 --> 03:39.950
Chiko?

67
03:41.159 --> 03:43.995
Long time no see! How have you been?

68
03:45.205 --> 03:48.542
You never reach out.

69
03:49.209 --> 03:52.504
Kataoka misses you, you know.

70
03:52.587 --> 03:53.838
Who misses her?

71
03:53.922 --> 03:55.507
[Hironi] It's you, little Kataoka.

72
03:55.590 --> 03:58.009
-[Chiko's friend] Cute, right? -Shut up, idiots!

73
03:58.093 --> 04:03.223
By the way, remember when Yusaku introduced you as his girl?

74
04:03.306 --> 04:06.560
-[Kataoka chuckles] -He glared at me

75
04:06.643 --> 04:09.396
-right off the bat. -[Hironi laughs]

76
04:09.479 --> 04:10.897
Like this.

77
04:10.981 --> 04:13.358
Had an attitude back then.

78
04:14.317 --> 04:15.569
Speaking of that... [clears throat]

79
04:15.652 --> 04:17.487
...where's Yusaku?

80
04:17.571 --> 04:18.613
Dunno.

81
04:18.697 --> 04:22.200
[Hironi] Left his apartment. Total ghost.

82
04:22.576 --> 04:24.035
Still in Osaka?

83
04:24.452 --> 04:27.581
[Hironi] Who knows. Should show his face after prison.

84
04:28.039 --> 04:29.332
[Chiko's friend] Right.

85
04:30.876 --> 04:32.127
[Kataoka sighs]

86
04:37.132 --> 04:39.843
So, you're Chiko's new guy?

87
04:40.427 --> 04:41.428
Yes.

88
04:42.971 --> 04:47.058
You look so pathetic.

89
04:47.851 --> 04:49.853
[Kataoka] Yusaku was way better.

90
04:49.936 --> 04:50.979
Leave him alone.

91
04:51.062 --> 04:53.815
[chuckles] Whatever, drink up!

92
04:54.357 --> 04:55.567
-Wait. -Bottoms up!

93
04:55.650 --> 04:57.861
You can't drink. Don't force it.

94
04:57.944 --> 04:59.779
[Kataoka] You don't drink either?

95
04:59.863 --> 05:02.490
Such a useless punk!

96
05:02.574 --> 05:04.492
Well, cheers!

97
05:04.576 --> 05:06.036
-That's the way. -Whoa!

98
05:07.412 --> 05:10.665
-[Chiko's friends exclaiming] -[gulping]

99
05:10.749 --> 05:11.750
It's so good!

100
05:11.833 --> 05:14.502
-Hell yeah! Look at him! -[exclaims]

101
05:14.586 --> 05:17.339
-[Kataoka] All right. -[Hironi] Go for more.

102
05:17.422 --> 05:21.676
-[chuckles] -You look like a total idiot.

103
05:21.760 --> 05:25.055
I have to say I'm a huge dumbass!

104
05:25.138 --> 05:26.306
-[smacks] -I know, idiot.

105
05:26.389 --> 05:27.557
[Satoshi gasping]

106
05:27.641 --> 05:29.976
Proud of it?

107
05:30.060 --> 05:32.896
You're just like Yusaku,

108
05:32.979 --> 05:35.899
making zero cash anyway.

109
05:35.982 --> 05:38.276
-Total idiot. -[Kataoka] Yeah.

110
05:38.360 --> 05:41.780
[Chiko's friend] He's real next-level stupid.

111
05:41.863 --> 05:44.616
What are you saying?

112
05:45.116 --> 05:49.329
Yusaku's a dumbass! [chuckles]

113
05:52.707 --> 05:54.292
Huh? [grunts]

114
05:55.919 --> 05:58.254
[Kataoka] What the hell do you know about him?

115
05:58.338 --> 06:00.340
[♪ tense music playing]

116
06:00.423 --> 06:03.718
He's a dumbass for real,

117
06:04.386 --> 06:08.014
but he'll jump into danger for Chiko without a second thought.

118
06:09.474 --> 06:11.685
[Kataoka] You got that kind of guts?

119
06:11.768 --> 06:14.521
-Stop! -[Chiko's friend] Relax, just watch.

120
06:16.439 --> 06:18.858
I... [splutters]

121
06:20.151 --> 06:22.320
Such a chicken.

122
06:22.654 --> 06:24.280
Say something!

123
06:24.823 --> 06:27.242
[grunting weakly]

124
06:28.284 --> 06:30.620
[splutters] I...

125
06:30.704 --> 06:33.707
[raises voice] I'll protect Chiko!

126
06:33.790 --> 06:35.041
[♪ music fades]

127
06:41.631 --> 06:44.175
[Hironi] Gosh. [chuckles]

128
06:44.843 --> 06:47.095
[Kataoka laughing]

129
06:47.679 --> 06:49.014
[thuds]

130
06:49.097 --> 06:51.015
[Chiko] Satoshi! You...

131
06:51.099 --> 06:53.059
You all right?

132
06:53.143 --> 06:55.687
-Get it together! -Screw Yusaku!

133
06:55.770 --> 06:57.522
I'll take him on anytime.

134
06:58.189 --> 06:59.941
-[Kataoka] Move, Chiko. -[Satoshi] Chiko!

135
07:00.024 --> 07:02.527
[breathing heavily]

136
07:02.610 --> 07:03.611
[Satoshi gasps]

137
07:05.905 --> 07:09.617
What can you do?

138
07:10.285 --> 07:12.495
The best you can do

139
07:12.579 --> 07:15.749
is crawl and cling to her!

140
07:18.084 --> 07:19.544
Just so you know,

141
07:20.295 --> 07:22.422
I'll do anything...

142
07:22.505 --> 07:25.717
I'll do whatever I can just to be with Chiko!

143
07:25.800 --> 07:27.427
Will you?

144
07:27.510 --> 07:29.763
Yeah? Then prove it, you pathetic--

145
07:29.846 --> 07:31.181
[Satoshi exclaims]

146
07:31.264 --> 07:33.141
[panting]

147
07:35.643 --> 07:36.770
[Kataoka groaning]

148
07:36.853 --> 07:39.939
[Chiko] Satoshi, you okay? Get up!

149
07:40.732 --> 07:43.568
[exclaims] You guys really went at it.

150
07:43.651 --> 07:44.861
[Kataoka] Shut up.

151
07:44.944 --> 07:47.947
[chuckles] Wait, you're bleeding?

152
07:48.323 --> 07:49.491
Damn it.

153
07:51.993 --> 07:52.994
Hey, Chiko.

154
07:54.579 --> 07:57.999
Don't you give a damn about Yusaku anymore?

155
08:00.376 --> 08:03.171
He might be suffering out there all alone.

156
08:03.254 --> 08:06.090
[♪ pensive music playing]

157
08:06.174 --> 08:07.884
I'll never forget him.

158
08:09.302 --> 08:10.303
But right now,

159
08:11.429 --> 08:13.723
my only focus is this guy.

160
08:16.518 --> 08:19.229
[Chiko's friend] Let's go. Get up.

161
08:19.312 --> 08:22.524
[Kataoka groaning] Piece of cake, idiots.

162
08:22.607 --> 08:24.359
-[Chiko's friend] You reek of puke! -[Kataoka] Shut up!

163
08:26.653 --> 08:27.737
Sorry about that.

164
08:29.197 --> 08:31.866
I didn't mean to stir things up.

165
08:32.951 --> 08:38.414
Though, if he could pull that off sober, I'd hand it to him.

166
08:40.667 --> 08:42.752
Satoshi, let's go.

167
08:43.545 --> 08:46.464
[Satoshi groans] Chiko, my head is killing me.

168
08:48.091 --> 08:50.593
Sorry for always being like this, Chiko.

169
08:50.677 --> 08:52.220
[Chiko] Yeah, I know.

170
08:52.762 --> 08:55.223
[Satoshi] Stay with me forever!

171
08:56.266 --> 08:57.559
[Chiko] I'm here.

172
08:59.269 --> 09:00.436
Come back again!

173
09:09.028 --> 09:10.155
[Satoshi] Oh.

174
09:10.572 --> 09:13.199
Working with Mr. Inaba today for the first time in forever.

175
09:14.450 --> 09:16.494
[Chiko] Ah, Satoshi.

176
09:17.537 --> 09:19.914
This is my share of the rent for this month.

177
09:19.998 --> 09:24.252
Huh? It's my room anyway. You don't have to go this far.

178
09:24.836 --> 09:27.922
[Chiko] We're living together, so paying half is only right.

179
09:30.550 --> 09:33.052
-Really? Well then... -Mm.

180
09:35.638 --> 09:38.516
[Satoshi exclaims] I'm broke again this month.

181
09:39.267 --> 09:41.227
I have to work harder.

182
09:41.853 --> 09:45.273
Just do your best. Weren't you the "do-anything idiot"?

183
09:45.356 --> 09:46.441
[Satoshi] Mm.

184
09:47.108 --> 09:49.569
-What? -Tell you later.

185
09:50.445 --> 09:52.447
Chiko, a goodbye kiss?

186
09:54.240 --> 09:56.576
We're in public, you perverted monkey.

187
10:00.205 --> 10:01.664
I guess not.

188
10:07.253 --> 10:08.796
Chiko!

189
10:15.053 --> 10:17.889
[Satoshi] White 956, moving out.

190
10:18.389 --> 10:19.390
[Inaba] Copy.

191
10:19.849 --> 10:20.975
ALTERNATING ONE-WAY

192
10:31.903 --> 10:33.613
[driver] Thanks, see you later.

193
10:33.696 --> 10:36.282
-Thank you too. -[engine revving]

194
10:44.624 --> 10:45.833
[Satoshi] Thank you for today.

195
10:45.917 --> 10:47.961
Satoshi, great work today.

196
10:48.711 --> 10:51.172
It was longer and tougher than expected, right?

197
10:51.256 --> 10:52.257
It was.

198
10:52.340 --> 10:55.093
Well, Mr. Inaba, I need to talk to you about something.

199
10:56.135 --> 10:57.720
[Inaba] Why are you suddenly serious?

200
10:57.804 --> 10:59.806
Well, actually,

201
10:59.889 --> 11:03.559
I've decided to quit this job and start looking for a real career.

202
11:05.353 --> 11:07.605
-Really? -Yes.

203
11:12.986 --> 11:16.239
It's not much, but happy graduation!

204
11:16.322 --> 11:17.532
You didn't have to.

205
11:17.615 --> 11:19.033
Thanks for everything.

206
11:19.409 --> 11:21.452
-I'm sorry. -[can clicks, fizzes]

207
11:21.536 --> 11:22.662
Well...

208
11:22.745 --> 11:23.746
Thank you.

209
11:23.830 --> 11:25.707
You're still young, Satoshi.

210
11:25.790 --> 11:28.501
You have to go explore what you're capable of.

211
11:28.584 --> 11:32.380
Well, "exploring potential" might be a stretch.

212
11:32.463 --> 11:36.259
If I'm gonna be with Chiko, I figured I need to get my act together.

213
11:36.342 --> 11:39.304
So, get a job and maybe get married?

214
11:39.887 --> 11:42.265
Married? Us?

215
11:42.348 --> 11:43.808
Of course!

216
11:43.891 --> 11:45.601
A couple living together

217
11:45.685 --> 11:47.270
bumping uglies night and day...

218
11:47.353 --> 11:49.272
Paths like that tend to open up.

219
11:49.731 --> 11:52.442
[chuckles] Married?

220
11:54.569 --> 11:57.196
[♪ cheery music playing]

221
12:01.951 --> 12:04.245
[Chiko] What's all this? What's going on?

222
12:04.329 --> 12:07.498
Well, I'm quitting my part-time job and getting a real job!

223
12:07.582 --> 12:10.293
[Satoshi sucks teeth] All right.

224
12:10.376 --> 12:14.130
What kind of a company should I choose?

225
12:14.213 --> 12:15.715
Watch me!

226
12:29.687 --> 12:30.980
This side's done.

227
12:31.898 --> 12:33.983
Then we're done for the day.

228
12:34.984 --> 12:36.486
Slow week?

229
12:39.489 --> 12:40.698
[Chiko's mom] Look at this.

230
12:48.956 --> 12:51.125
Getting a new CNC lathe machine?

231
12:51.209 --> 12:52.794
It's used, though.

232
12:53.544 --> 12:56.339
A tiny workshop like ours

233
12:56.798 --> 13:00.051
has to take on the fussy jobs others reject, right?

234
13:00.134 --> 13:01.552
That's it.

235
13:01.844 --> 13:05.681
If we can run this through the night, we can take on jobs we couldn't before.

236
13:06.766 --> 13:08.601
Where'd you get the money for that?

237
13:08.684 --> 13:11.562
I'll scrape it together somehow.

238
13:12.188 --> 13:15.900
This is when we go on the offensive.

239
13:17.402 --> 13:19.404
Then I'll pitch in a bit more at home.

240
13:19.487 --> 13:20.613
Idiot!

241
13:21.280 --> 13:22.782
I'm not gonna leech off a kid.

242
13:23.116 --> 13:25.076
Don't worry about it.

243
13:34.001 --> 13:35.211
[Chiko] Got bored already?

244
13:36.504 --> 13:39.841
[Satoshi] None of these click.

245
13:40.716 --> 13:44.011
I'm starting to wonder what I'm even capable of doing.

246
13:46.472 --> 13:49.142
How about this? "Immediate hiring. Sales role."

247
13:50.226 --> 13:52.979
No way, I'm terrible at talking to people.

248
13:55.731 --> 13:58.151
This one, a construction job.

249
13:59.735 --> 14:03.364
Got a hernia, and if I push it, my asthma acts up.

250
14:04.031 --> 14:06.659
Bad at cooking,

251
14:06.742 --> 14:09.036
and I can hardly touch a computer.

252
14:09.829 --> 14:12.248
Do you actually want a job?

253
14:13.124 --> 14:14.667
Of course I do!

254
14:14.750 --> 14:17.503
Then call somewhere, anywhere!

255
14:19.130 --> 14:20.464
[Satoshi] Yeah. [sighs]

256
14:22.508 --> 14:23.509
[Chiko tuts]

257
14:24.302 --> 14:27.430
[Chiko breathing heavily]

258
14:28.806 --> 14:30.224
-[smacks] -[Chiko grunts angrily]

259
14:35.605 --> 14:38.024
[Satoshi] That's a blue-collar job magazine.

260
14:38.816 --> 14:40.568
Why are you suddenly looking too?

261
14:40.651 --> 14:42.361
Not sudden at all.

262
14:42.445 --> 14:44.655
I said before I wanted to be a driver.

263
14:47.700 --> 14:48.784
[sighs]

264
14:51.162 --> 14:54.081
It's so good you know what you want to do.

265
14:55.291 --> 14:58.753
Something you want to do? Don't be so spoiled.

266
14:58.836 --> 15:00.213
Just do what you can.

267
15:00.713 --> 15:03.966
Forgot how brutal job hunting was back in high school?

268
15:06.260 --> 15:09.680
Back then, I'd get nervous and get diarrhea!

269
15:10.765 --> 15:13.059
But meeting Chiko changed me!

270
15:13.142 --> 15:14.852
[friend] 'Cause you lost your virginity?

271
15:14.936 --> 15:18.272
-I'll fillet you like a fish. -[groans] It's not like that!

272
15:19.982 --> 15:22.944
But if I do nothing,

273
15:23.444 --> 15:24.946
she'll leave me in the dust.

274
15:25.029 --> 15:27.907
Eiji-kun, take care of this too.

275
15:27.990 --> 15:28.991
[Eiji] Sure!

276
15:33.204 --> 15:38.209
Biologically speaking, you and Chiko are totally different species.

277
15:38.709 --> 15:42.129
A garnish and a tuna steak will never be equal anyway.

278
15:42.505 --> 15:45.049
So a garnish should just accept being thrown away?

279
15:45.549 --> 15:46.634
[Eiji] Mm...

280
15:47.927 --> 15:49.136
Here, look at me.

281
15:50.096 --> 15:53.557
When I was a kid, I didn't look up to male staff here

282
15:53.641 --> 15:55.893
and dream of working at a supermarket.

283
15:56.477 --> 15:59.021
But you have to do what you have to do.

284
15:59.605 --> 16:02.858
Once you try, you might see things differently.

285
16:06.445 --> 16:07.738
Young man!

286
16:08.447 --> 16:11.826
Stick a discount sticker on this too!

287
16:11.909 --> 16:16.664
Can't beat these old ladies. Hang on. Don't tell anyone, okay?

288
16:18.165 --> 16:19.750
[Satoshi's mom] Fits perfectly.

289
16:20.334 --> 16:22.128
Your dad would be happy too.

290
16:22.211 --> 16:25.423
Too soon! I haven't even had an interview yet.

291
16:26.007 --> 16:27.675
Stop complaining and take it.

292
16:28.801 --> 16:31.220
Why do you tie like that? Let me see.

293
16:32.263 --> 16:33.264
Well...

294
16:35.975 --> 16:38.352
If you don't get a proper job this time,

295
16:38.811 --> 16:40.187
you're banned from this house.

296
16:41.605 --> 16:43.941
You're gonna be an uncle soon.

297
16:44.025 --> 16:45.401
Get your act together!

298
16:52.825 --> 16:54.285
[Yasushi] I'll do it.

299
16:54.368 --> 16:56.245
Fold it neatly edge-to-edge.

300
16:56.329 --> 16:57.455
[Yasushi] Got it.

301
16:58.748 --> 17:00.875
[Sayaka] Redo that one.

302
17:06.380 --> 17:08.007
I'm home.

303
17:10.551 --> 17:12.553
Okay, goodbye.

304
17:15.723 --> 17:17.224
[Satoshi] Any luck?

305
17:17.308 --> 17:21.020
Most places require a license held for over a year.

306
17:21.520 --> 17:22.730
I see. [sighs]

307
17:22.813 --> 17:25.483
Well, I'll just keep looking until I find one.

308
17:46.003 --> 17:47.046
[Satoshi sighs]

309
17:57.223 --> 17:58.265
[phone ringing]

310
17:58.349 --> 18:00.393
Oh! It's the security company.

311
18:00.476 --> 18:02.061
[breathing nervously] Huh?

312
18:03.688 --> 18:05.356
Hello. What happened?

313
18:07.358 --> 18:08.401
Huh?

314
18:09.110 --> 18:11.779
Chiko, Mr. Inaba collapsed!

315
18:12.530 --> 18:14.865
-[splutters] What do you mean? -Huh?

316
18:16.617 --> 18:18.744
[Satoshi] He's now at the hospital, unconscious!

317
18:18.828 --> 18:22.081
What should I do? If anything happens to him...

318
18:22.164 --> 18:23.582
-How could I-- -Let's go.

319
18:37.430 --> 18:38.431
Come on.

320
19:03.998 --> 19:05.541
[Inaba laughs]

321
19:06.333 --> 19:09.879
Nah! Just malnutrition and sleep deprivation!

322
19:10.296 --> 19:12.173
IV isn't enough,

323
19:12.757 --> 19:15.342
so I'm bingeing on everyone's gifts!

324
19:15.426 --> 19:17.261
Satoshi was crying!

325
19:17.344 --> 19:18.596
I was not!

326
19:19.221 --> 19:20.848
Sorry for worrying you guys.

327
19:20.931 --> 19:23.768
But I'm glad to see both of you.

328
19:24.101 --> 19:27.563
How's life? Still going strong in both ways?

329
19:27.646 --> 19:29.899
Stop talking nonsense.

330
19:29.982 --> 19:32.026
[chuckles] Right!

331
19:32.693 --> 19:36.906
Why not have a beauty here peel an apple for me?

332
19:36.989 --> 19:39.408
-Here. -[Chiko] I'm terrible at this.

333
19:42.953 --> 19:45.456
Is this because I left?

334
19:45.539 --> 19:48.209
Did you overwork because you were short-staffed?

335
19:48.292 --> 19:49.668
No.

336
19:49.752 --> 19:52.171
I might not look it, but I'm twice divorced. Mm.

337
19:52.797 --> 19:55.341
I've got plenty of red flags, and I'm working hard

338
19:55.925 --> 19:59.929
to build up my kids' savings.

339
20:00.012 --> 20:03.724
That's my whatchamacallit... eye-den...

340
20:03.808 --> 20:07.102
Eye-den... tit-tee!

341
20:08.395 --> 20:09.814
Maybe that's the wrong word.

342
20:09.897 --> 20:10.981
[Inaba] Is it?

343
20:11.065 --> 20:15.402
Anyway, never feel guilty for no reason.

344
20:16.695 --> 20:19.448
Then, until you recover, I can--

345
20:19.532 --> 20:21.867
I told you. I'm fine!

346
20:21.951 --> 20:24.078
Just do what you want, Satoshi.

347
20:24.161 --> 20:27.581
If it doesn't work out, you can always come back. Okay?

348
20:29.708 --> 20:30.876
Yes.

349
20:40.511 --> 20:42.847
[grunting]

350
20:48.185 --> 20:50.646
Damn! I told you I'm terrible at this!

351
20:50.729 --> 20:52.356
I didn't say a word! [chuckles]

352
20:52.439 --> 20:54.149
Screw this! I'm done!

353
20:54.233 --> 20:55.860
[Inaba and Satoshi chuckle]

354
20:55.943 --> 20:59.363
-[insects chirping] -[frog croaking]

355
21:06.495 --> 21:07.663
[Satoshi] Right here?

356
21:08.330 --> 21:10.541
This is where we became one!

357
21:11.333 --> 21:12.376
It's destiny!

358
21:13.335 --> 21:15.671
To be back here on a night like this is superb!

359
21:16.297 --> 21:17.882
Yeah, I agree.

360
21:25.264 --> 21:26.265
You know,

361
21:27.433 --> 21:29.685
my dad died from overwork.

362
21:32.396 --> 21:38.235
He came home, went to sleep, and just never woke up.

363
21:39.194 --> 21:41.280
[♪ gentle somber music playing]

364
21:47.786 --> 21:49.204
[groaning]

365
21:49.288 --> 21:52.458
Wh... What are you doing?

366
21:53.208 --> 21:55.836
I'll do my best! I'll try everything!

367
22:01.258 --> 22:02.968
If you don't get a job soon,

368
22:04.011 --> 22:05.888
I'll become a driver before you.

369
22:07.806 --> 22:09.183
[Satoshi] Wait, no!

370
22:09.266 --> 22:12.269
I'm gonna find a job, work my ass off,

371
22:12.353 --> 22:14.521
and stay with you forever,

372
22:14.605 --> 22:15.606
and then...

373
22:17.691 --> 22:20.027
And then what?

374
22:21.236 --> 22:22.321
I will...

375
22:26.992 --> 22:27.993
for now...

376
22:28.869 --> 22:30.913
be running all the way home!

377
22:31.455 --> 22:34.083
-Huh? What? -I'll start first!

378
22:36.293 --> 22:39.380
[Satoshi shouts]

379
22:39.463 --> 22:40.839
[grunting]

380
22:41.423 --> 22:42.508
[chuckles]

381
22:46.929 --> 22:49.431
[Satoshi shouts]

382
22:49.515 --> 22:50.516
Real idiot.

383
22:52.101 --> 22:54.311
[Satoshi shouts] I can do this!

384
22:56.313 --> 22:58.691
[Satoshi] I saw the job ad.

385
22:59.525 --> 23:02.403
Yes, my name is Yanagawa.

386
23:03.028 --> 23:04.613
Right.

387
23:05.322 --> 23:07.199
I'm 23.

388
23:07.282 --> 23:09.535
Moriguchi City.

389
23:10.119 --> 23:13.288
-Yes, hello? -For now, I only have a semi license.

390
23:13.372 --> 23:15.332
-Interview? Of course. -Yes.

391
23:15.416 --> 23:17.001
-Yes. -Yes.

392
23:17.084 --> 23:19.837
-So, see you tomorrow. -Then, see you tomorrow.

393
23:23.340 --> 23:24.341
Got it too?

394
23:24.425 --> 23:25.718
I got an interview!

395
23:26.135 --> 23:27.219
How about you, Chiko?

396
23:27.678 --> 23:30.055
[excited gasp] It's destiny.

397
23:31.223 --> 23:33.475
-[Satoshi] Destiny! -[Chiko] We haven't passed yet.

398
23:34.018 --> 23:35.019
Go easy on it.

399
23:36.812 --> 23:41.734
OSAKA'S TOP FOOD PICK, KUSHIKATSU (DEEP-FRIED SKEWERS)

400
23:41.817 --> 23:44.069
[sizzling]

401
23:48.407 --> 23:49.992
[crunching]

402
23:52.327 --> 23:53.328
This is good.

403
23:54.663 --> 23:56.665
[indistinct chatter]

404
23:59.710 --> 24:01.211
[Eiji] Nothing beats this place.

405
24:01.295 --> 24:02.880
MATSUI NO DOUBLE-DIPPING

406
24:02.963 --> 24:05.382
[♪ closing theme music playing]

407
24:05.382 --> 24:06.382
MkvDrama.net
